{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: don't anchor a parity-slice boundary on `assert`**

`assert(assemblyStart >= 0, ...)` guards the `wiring.substring(assemblyStart)` slice, but `assert` bodies are stripped when assertions are disabled — the guard then vanishes and a moved `_buildCoreTools` signature fails with a raw `RangeError` from `substring(-1)` instead of the helpful "tool assembly moved — update the parity slice" message. `dart test` / `flutter test` run with asserts on so this is latent only, but the parity tests are precisely the long-lived tripwires — prefer a guard that cannot be compiled away:

```dart
if (assemblyStart < 0) {
  fail('host_agent_wiring.dart: tool assembly moved — update the parity slice');
